INTRODUCTION
Metal(loid)s are among the most common chemical
contaminants present in the environment, occurring in water,
soil, and air through both natural processes and anthropogenic activities. Human exposure may occur via inhalation,
ingestion of contaminated water and food, dermal contact,
occupational activities, and exposure to contaminated soil,
dust, and air (Carlin et al., 2016; Mohammadi-Moghadam et
al., 2022). Toxic metal(loid)s, such as lead (Pb), mercury
(Hg), cadmium (Cd), arsenic (As), and chromium (Cr), are
